// Detection: Password spraying from a single IP
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1110.003 Brute Force: Password Spraying (tactic: Credential Access, TA0006)
// Severity: Medium
// Logic: one IP fails sign-in (ResultType 50126) on many different accounts within one hour,
//        with almost no successful sign-ins from that IP in the same hour.
// Thresholds: at least 10 distinct accounts and a success rate below 10%.
//        The busiest office hour reached 15 distinct accounts, but with about 94% success,
//        so the success-rate filter removes it.
// Known false positives: a shared office or proxy IP right after a company-wide password reset.
// Limits: an attacker who spreads attempts over many hours or many IPs can stay below the threshold.
SigninLogs
| summarize Attempts = count(), Successes = countif(ResultType == "0"), Failures = countif(ResultType == "50126"), DistinctUsers = dcountif(UserPrincipalName, ResultType == "50126") by IPAddress, bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)
| extend SuccessRate = round(100.0 * Successes / Attempts, 1)
| where DistinctUsers >= 10 and SuccessRate < 10
| sort by DistinctUsers desc